
                                CHANGELOG
                                =========
0.1.0 - March 2006
------------------
Initial alpha release

0.9.0 - April 2006
------------------
First beta release. Lots of additions and changes from 0.1.0

1.0.0 - April 2006
------------------
- Implemented multidimensional arrays (previously only 1D)
- Changed ENDIF to FI (I decided ENDIF was too long winded)
- Added CURSOR, (standalone) BREAK & INDENT commands
- Added MAX(), MIN(), MAX$(), MIN$(), TOSTR$(), WAITDATA(), UPPER$(), LOWER$()
  functions
- MID$(), LEFT$(), RIGHT$() now accept zero length
- Added argc and argv$() system variables
- Added file permissions argument to OPEN command
- Added -nobreak command line option 
- Removed -noindent command line option (it was fairly pointless)
- SIGQUIT now handled
- Internal changes

1.1.0 - May 2006
----------------
- Added PAGING command
- Added REVERSE$() function

1.2.0 - June 2006
-----------------
- Added non (BASIC) standard CHOOSE/CHOSEN structure which has the same logic
  as switch() in C. CHOOSE sounds nicer to me and more intuitive than calling
  it SWITCH.
- Changed the operation of the FOR loop - stepping always defaults to 1 and
  loop will not now run if stepping does not match loop direction implied by
  start and end values.
- Added SORT command which sorts numeric and string 1D arrays
- Added MATCH(), MEAN(), GMEAN(), MEDIAN() functions
- Added ARMAX(), ARMIN(), ARMEAN(), ARGMEAN(), ARMEDIAN() functions
- Added ARMAX$(), ARMIN$()
- Added SWAPCASE$()
- Added ABS(), FLOOR(), CEIL()
- Added ISUPPER(), ISLOWER(), ISALPHA(), ISALNUM(), ISDIGIT(), ISBLANK(),
        ISPRINT(), ISPUNCT()

1.2.1 - June 2006
-----------------
- Mods for Solaris
- Fixed minor bug in isNumeric() function - it thought "." was a valid float.

1.2.2 - July 2006
-----------------
- Added GETENV$() function which returns the values of enviroment variables.
  There is no corresponding setenv yet as it would serve no purpose since
  BASIC cannot yet spawn child processes.
- Added ENVEXISTS()
- Other minor code updates.
